  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Seed Roadmap Update</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to build upon the experiences and lessons learned in the Collaborative Seed Programme (CSP) and prepare for its successor/s, thereby evaluating gaps, updating the Nigerian National Seed Road Map (NSRM) and its dashboard for monitoring seed sector development, building coalitions, and deepening interests in farmer- and community managed seed systems, the potato sub-sector, and of Dutch private sector. The updated NSRM and momentum generated in organizing stakeholders into coalitions contributing to its vision will guide future investments, priorities, and collaborations in Nigeria&#x2019;s seed sector, including in a potential second phase of CSP. The project will strengthen the position of the updated NSRM, coalitions, and CSP-II in coordinating seed sector development. In addition, the results will contribute to EKN Nigeria&#x2019;s investment strategy on how and where investments can be made with a view to developing the horticulture and potato sectors in North and Southwest Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
